Ultimately, Mr Miller, Nethack is just a game.  It does not control
infrastructure or safety-critical systems. It does not process people's
taxes, filter their inbound e-mail for spam, dispense their medication,
or monitor the instruments of their nuclear power stations.

As such, I see no grounds for saying that the Dev Team's conduct in this
matter - assembling a closed team of people whose personalities and
coding styles they find congenial - does any meaningful harm.
